# CD+Tests: Codex MCP guided inspection

Decision: revise

Implementation is complete for the approved Core slice; native qualification is blocked by the approved execution guard composition. This is not a QA pass.

## Implementation and source binding

The shared inspection contract exposes its unchanged conditions under dependentSchemas.operation, reuses one selector conversion map and preserves required operation/unknown-field rejection. Core service constructs explicitly bound sequential read hints from existing command/catalog owners, preserves original document revisions, keeps current contract revisions, and contains only advisory navigation failures through one legacy report/presentation path. Production changes stay in contract.js and service.js; regressions use the two registered CLI/protocol test files.

The original source base is 5046858826f3bca7922c14ef402b095feca8b6fb. evidence/build/source-bindings.json proves actual workspace Core resolution and exact assembled Core bytes. evidence/build/frozen-candidate.json binds 19,336 candidate files. The retained preflight confirms that candidate remains unchanged. Canonical generated compatibility changes contain 56 deterministic scenarios with zero unexpected failures and no new native qualification claims.

