## Native execution and concrete blocker

The first model-free wrapper attempt timed out in an overbroad Root filesystem snapshot before guard/harness launch. Its setup failure is retained. The corrected snapshot covers tracked/nonignored Root files and the complete control tree required by TP; the whole-ROOT OS write denial is unchanged. The corrected preflight actually verifies ROOT write denial, then the unchanged native harness fails before Codex login status can execute: nested sandbox application is refused with exit 71. The original broad account-error observation and the independent exact-stack diagnostic are retained unchanged/separately. No discovery result or account invalidity is inferred from that error.

Both before/after snapshots match across 14,038 Root files, global settings and staging. All 19,336 frozen candidate files match. No credentials were copied or inspected, no login, plugin/global installation or global-setting change occurred, no API provider fallback was used, and no model session or cohort slot was consumed/reserved. Exactly two fresh qualifying sessions remain required and unfulfilled. No additional launch is attempted under a weaker or substituted guard.

## Task fulfillment and routing

T-BASE, T-RET, T-CORE, T-NAV, T-SCHEMA, T-RENDER and T-BUILD have their above evidence. T-NATIVE is blocked before model execution. Dependent review/QA/UAT/OR readiness is not asserted. No commit, push, PR, merge, installation or release occurred.

Finding NATIVE-GUARD-001: emergent_risk; routing_target: SD; owner: existing native-harness execution owner / sd-definition. The approved outer-plus-existing-inner guard is incompatible with this host. GUARD_REVISION_PROPOSAL.md describes a single combined OS policy retaining every denial, unchanged task/audit and the same two-session budget. SD's unchanged-guard statement and dependent TP/fingerprints require deliberate canonical renewal before native qualification. UR/PRD acceptance is not narrowed.

Read BROWNFIELD_ANALYSIS_CLARIFICATION.md with the original analysis: the selected route remains structured_delivery. The analysis's slice label was a transcription error, not a route change or omitted gate.
